# Backend Engineering Rules

These rules govern backend code changes when using AI tools.

## 1. Tech Stack Assumptions
- Django
- Django REST Framework
- GraphQL (where applicable)
- PostgreSQL
- AWS (Lambda, Batch, S3, DynamoDB)
- Sentry enabled

---

## 2. Core Principles
- Correctness > performance > elegance
- ORM-first (raw SQL only when unavoidable)
- Idempotent operations
- Safe for large datasets

---

## 3. Query Rules (CRITICAL)
- No N+1 queries
- Always use:
  - `select_related` for FK
  - `prefetch_related` for M2M / reverse FK
- Use annotations instead of Python loops
- Paginate all list APIs

---

## 4. Serialization Rules
- Prefer:
  - DRF Serializers
  - or GraphQL resolvers
- Avoid manual `for` loops building response dicts
- Computed fields must be annotated in queryset if possible

---

## 5. Transaction & Update Rules
- Use `transaction.atomic()` where needed
- Bulk update when possible
- Avoid per-row updates inside loops

---

## 6. Logging Rules
- Use structured logging
- Log levels:
  - INFO: flow-level
  - DEBUG: per-record
  - WARNING: data issues
  - ERROR: failures with IDs
- Never log PII

---

## 7. Script Rules (One-off / Migration Scripts)
- Must support **dry-run by default**
- Must be idempotent
- Must log:
  - total records found
  - total updated
  - skipped records

---

## 8. Environment Handling
- No hardcoded environment names
- Accept env at runtime:
  - local / dev / stage / prod
- Environment name == DB name

---

## 9. Error Handling
- Fail loudly but safely
- Catch and log exceptions with identifiers
- Never swallow exceptions silently

---

## 10. Performance Expectations
- Avoid loading entire tables into memory
- Use batching / iterators
- Avoid serializer misuse in loops

---

## 11. Sentry & Monitoring
- Assume Sentry is active
- Fix:
  - N+1 queries
  - slow spans
  - repeated updates
- Any Sentry fix must include explanation

---

## 12. Documentation & Commit Rules (Mandatory)
Every backend change must include:
- Inline code comments (why, not what)
- Documentation update if behavior changes
- Commit message

### Commit Message Format
- feat(backend): short meaningful description
- fix(backend): issue resolved
- refactor(backend): code cleanup
- perf(backend): query or runtime optimization
- chore(backend): tooling or infra


---

## 13. AI Interaction Rule
AI output must:
- Explain query changes
- Highlight performance impact
- Mention backward compatibility
- Be safe for production usage
